[32m+[m[32m### D-024: Risk-free rate conversion[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Status:** Accepted · **Proposed by:** Claude Code (milestone 1) · **Date:** 2026-10-13[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Decision:** an annual risk-free rate R is converted to a periodic rate with geometric[m
[32m+[m[32m  compounding, r_f = (1 + R)^(1/N) − 1, before it is subtracted from periodic returns.[m
[32m+[m[32m  `sharpe_ratio` accepts either `annual_risk_free_rate` (scalar) or `periodic_risk_free_rate`[m
[32m+[m[32m  (scalar or series), never both; the default is 0.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Rationale:** compounding N periodic rates reproduces R exactly. This matches the config field[m
[32m+[m[32m  `environment.risk_free_rate`, which is an annual decimal.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Alternative:** simple division R / N, which is common and slightly larger. For R = 2 % and[m
[32m+[m[32m  N = 252, simple division gives 7.937 × 10⁻⁵ and geometric gives 7.858 × 10⁻⁵ per day. The[m
[32m+[m[32m  difference (about 7.8 × 10⁻⁷ per day) is small, but the choice is stated for reproducibility.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Approved by / date:** team member using Git identity `Parvptl`, Claude Code session of 2026-10-13.[m
