[32m+[m[32m### D-025: Behaviour for undefined metrics[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Status:** Accepted · **Proposed by:** Claude Code (milestone 1) · **Date:** 2026-10-13[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Decision:** a mathematically undefined metric raises `UndefinedMetricError` (a subclass of[m
[32m+[m[32m  `ValueError`). Currently this is a Sharpe ratio whose excess-return std is zero. The function never[m
[32m+[m[32m  returns `inf`, `nan` or a substitute value. Callers that build result tables catch the error and[m
[32m+[m[32m  record "undefined" explicitly.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Tolerance:** a periodic sample std ≤ `ZERO_VOLATILITY_TOLERANCE` = 1e-12 counts as zero, so[m
[32m+[m[32m  that floating-point noise (~1e-18) on constant series cannot produce ratios of ~1e16. Volatility[m
[32m+[m[32m  is reported as exactly 0.0 under the same rule.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Alternative:** returning NaN, which is a widespread convention but propagates silently through[m
[32m+[m[32m  averages and tables.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Tolerance review (2026-10-13), kept at 1e-12.** Measured on this machine (NumPy 2.5.4):[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Noise std of mathematically constant series with values 1e-6 to 0.1 and lengths 2 to 25 200:[m
[32m+[m[32m    at most ~2.8 × 10⁻¹⁷. Exact zero for values 1 to 100 in that test.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Noise std of `r − rf` with constant difference (2 000 random trials): at most ~1.3 × 10⁻¹⁸.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Smallest realistic periodic std, from daily T-bill-like returns with the rate drifting from[m
[32m+[m[32m    4 % to 5 % p.a.: ~1.1 × 10⁻⁵.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - So 1e-12 is about 5 orders of magnitude above the observed noise and about 7 below realistic[m
[32m+[m[32m    volatility.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Limitations:**[m
[32m+[m[32m  - The tolerance is absolute, not relative to the size of the returns.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - A genuine standard deviation below 1e-12 would be reported as zero volatility, making the[m
[32m+[m[32m    Sharpe ratio undefined.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Noise grows roughly with return magnitude × machine epsilon (~2.2 × 10⁻¹⁶). It could[m
[32m+[m[32m    approach 1e-12 only for returns of order 10³ or more, which are not realistic decimal returns.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - The measurements are empirical, from one platform, not a proof.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Approved by / date:** team member using Git identity `Parvptl`, Claude Code session of 2026-10-13.[m
