[32m+[m[32m### D-026: Drawdown conventions[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Status:** Accepted · **Proposed by:** Claude Code (milestone 1) · **Date:** 2026-10-13[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Decision:** drawdown is measured from the running peak P_t = max_{s≤t} V_s, with the **first[m
[32m+[m[32m  observation as the initial peak**. Maximum drawdown is reported as a non-positive decimal, with[m
[32m+[m[32m  positional `peak_index` and `trough_index`.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Ties: the earliest deepest point is the trough; the latest observation at the running-peak level[m
[32m+[m[32m    before it is the peak.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - With no decline, the result is 0.0 and both indices are 0.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Consequence:** any drawdown already in progress at the start of an evaluation window is not[m
[32m+[m[32m  counted. Evaluation windows should be reported with this caveat.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Approved by / date:** team member using Git identity `Parvptl`, Claude Code session of 2026-10-13.[m
