[32m+[m[32m### D-029: Annualised return (geometric, CAGR)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Status:** Accepted · **Proposed by:** Claude Code (milestone 1) · **Date:** 2026-10-13[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Decision:** `annualized_return(portfolio_values, periods_per_year)` = (V_T / V_0)^(N/T) − 1.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - T is the number of return periods (number of values − 1).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - N is passed explicitly, as in D-023.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - At least one period is required.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - The result is computed as `expm1((N/T)·log(V_T/V_0))` for precision.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - A result too large to represent raises `ValueError`. Extreme short-period losses may round[m
[32m+[m[32m    to −1.0.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Why geometric:** it is the constant yearly growth rate that reproduces the realised outcome.[m
[32m+[m[32m  The arithmetic alternative mean(r_t) · N overstates compounded growth when returns vary[m
[32m+[m[32m  ("volatility drag", approximately σ²/2 per period). Example: +50 % then −50 % has an[m
[32m+[m[32m  arithmetic mean of 0 but a geometric rate of −13.4 % per period.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Known limitation, not solved:** annualising a short window extrapolates it. For example, one[m
[32m+[m[32m  month at +5 % annualises to ≈ +79.6 %. No minimum length is enforced in the function.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Reporting rule (accepted with this decision):** state T and the dates with every annualised[m
[32m+[m[32m  figure, and do not headline annualised returns for windows shorter than one year.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Consistency note:** the Sharpe ratio uses the *arithmetic* mean of excess returns (handbook[m
[32m+[m[32m  §10.4; D-022, D-024), so CAGR and the Sharpe numerator are different quantities by design.[m
[32m+[m[32m  Reports should not mix them.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Approved by / date:** team member using Git identity `Parvptl`, Claude Code session of 2026-10-13.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### D-030: Turnover input contract[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Status:** Accepted · **Proposed by:** Claude Code (milestone 1) · **Date:** 2026-10-13[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Decision:** `portfolio_turnover(pre_trade_weights, post_trade_weights, *, cash_column=None)`[m
[32m+[m[32m  takes two matrices of shape (events, assets) and returns a float64 array with one two-way value[m
[32m+[m[32m  per row, in [0, 2]. The measure is the all-column default, or traded notional if `cash_column` is[m
[32m+[m[32m  given (D-011).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - **Pre-trade weights** are the actual, drift-adjusted weights immediately before trading,[m
[32m+[m[32m    supplied by the caller. **Post-trade weights** are the target weights immediately after[m
[32m+[m[32m    trading.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - The function does not infer drift, dates or asset returns. Comparing consecutive targets is[m
[32m+[m[32m    wrong after drift; this is demonstrated in `tests/test_turnover.py`.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Same asset ordering in both matrices. Cash is a column if the portfolio can hold cash, so that[m
[32m+[m[32m    each row sums to 1.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - **Long-only only:** weights must be finite and ≥ 0, and each row must sum to 1 within[m
[32m+[m[32m    `WEIGHT_SUM_TOLERANCE = 1e-6`. This accepts float64/float32 rounding and rejects real[m
[32m+[m[32m    allocation errors such as an omitted cash column.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Initial funding from cash counts only if supplied as a row.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `ValueError` for: empty matrices; non-2-D input (a single event must have shape[m
[32m+[m[32m    (1, assets)); shape mismatch; non-finite, negative or non-summing weights.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `TypeError` for non-numeric or boolean weights.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Aggregation:** `annualized_turnover(event_turnover, observation_periods, periods_per_year)`[m
[32m+[m[32m  = Σ τ_k · N / T_obs.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - T_obs is the number of return periods in the evaluation window, independent of the number of[m
[32m+[m[32m    events.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - An empty event list means no trading and gives 0.0. This is a deliberate exception to the[m
[32m+[m[32m    "empty raises" rule, because zero events is a meaningful outcome (e.g. buy-and-hold).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Event values must be finite and in [0, 2], with an allowance of 2 × `WEIGHT_SUM_TOLERANCE`[m
[32m+[m[32m    above 2 for rounding; otherwise `ValueError`. 2-D input raises `ValueError`.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `observation_periods` must be a Python or NumPy integer (`TypeError` otherwise, booleans[m
[32m+[m[32m    included) and > 0 (`ValueError` otherwise).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `periods_per_year` is validated as for the other annualised metrics.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **`cash_column` (approved 2026-10-13):** optional, keyword-only, 0-based, non-negative index.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - The column is excluded from the sum but **not** from validation: complete rows, cash[m
[32m+[m[32m    included, must still be finite, non-negative and sum to 1.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Non-integers and booleans raise `TypeError`; indices outside [0, assets − 1], negative ones[m
[32m+[m[32m    included, raise `ValueError`.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - The function cannot verify that column j really is cash.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **`annualized_turnover` return type:** always a Python `float`, also for NumPy integer[m
[32m+[m[32m  `observation_periods` (fixed and regression-tested on 2026-10-13). The aggregate inherits the[m
[32m+[m[32m  measure of its input events.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Not handled:** short positions or leverage (would need a gross-exposure definition), and[m
[32m+[m[32m  cash flows into or out of the portfolio.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Approval record:** the `cash_column` extension was approved first, then the full contract[m
[32m+[m[32m  (input rules, `WEIGHT_SUM_TOLERANCE` = 1e-6, aggregation, empty-events rule). Before acceptance,[m
[32m+[m[32m  the wording was corrected on 2026-10-13 to match the code: the signature now shows[m
[32m+[m[32m  `cash_column`, `TypeError` and `ValueError` cases are separated, and the event-value range and[m
[32m+[m[32m  `observation_periods` rules are stated.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Approved by / date:** team member using Git identity `Parvptl`, Claude Code session of 2026-10-13.[m
