[32m+[m[32m### D-031: Turnover vs. transaction-cost basis[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Status:** Open · **Date raised:** 2026-10-13[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Context:** two-way turnover with a cash column counts both legs of a trade into or out of cash.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Example: buying 0.10 of an asset with cash gives τ = 0.20, but only 0.10 of a security is[m
[32m+[m[32m    actually traded.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Switching 0.10 between two assets gives τ = 0.20, and 0.20 of securities is traded.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - So "cost = cost_bps × τ × V" would double-charge cash-funded trades.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Options:**[m
[32m+[m[32m  - (a) Charge costs on non-cash legs only: Σ over non-cash assets of |Δw| × V.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - (b) Charge on τ / 2 (one-way).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - (c) Accept the asymmetry and document it.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Analysis (pre-commit review, 2026-10-13):** with cash as a column, one-way = max(B, S) ≤ traded[m
[32m+[m[32m  notional = B + S ≤ default two-way = 2·max(B, S). Neither turnover variant equals traded notional[m
[32m+[m[32m  in general. Charging costs on traded notional is the mathematically consistent choice.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Proposed direction (approved as direction, not implemented):**[m
[32m+[m[32m  - cost per rebalance = κ · n · V_pre, where n = `portfolio_turnover(..., cash_column=j)` and[m
[32m+[m[32m    κ = (transaction_cost_bps + slippage_bps) / 10⁴;[m
[32m+[m[32m  - the cost is deducted pro rata, which keeps post-trade weights on target, with a cost error of[m
[32m+[m[32m    at most κ · cost (second order).[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Still open:**[m
[32m+[m[32m  - implementation and validation in the environment milestone;[m
[32m+[m[32m  - which measure the config `max_turnover` cap constrains. The config comment currently describes[m
[32m+[m[32m    the default all-column measure; it was **not** changed.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **To decide** with the environment and cost model (milestones 4 and 7) before any cost-inclusive[m
[32m+[m[32m  result is reported. `portfolio_turnover` itself is not affected.[m
