[32m+[m[32m### 10.2 Portfolio returns: `portfolio_returns(portfolio_values)`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Purpose.** Converts a portfolio-value path, such as the output of a backtest, into period[m
[32m+[m[32m   returns. All other return-based metrics start from these.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Definition.** r_t = V_t / V_{t−1} − 1, for t = 1, …, n.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Variables.** V_t is the portfolio value at observation t, in any currency unit. r_t is the[m
[32m+[m[32m   simple (arithmetic) return over the period ending at t.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Assumptions and units.** Values are in chronological order. Values must be strictly positive:[m
[32m+[m[32m   V ≤ 0 means the portfolio is ruined or the input is invalid, so the return is undefined or[m
[32m+[m[32m   misleading. Output is in decimals.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Example.** V = [100, 110, 99, 99] gives r = [0.10, −0.10, 0.00]. Note that +10 % followed[m
[32m+[m[32m   by −10 % does not return to 100.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. **Contract.** Input: at least 2 finite, positive values. Output: a float64 NumPy array of length[m
[32m+[m[32m   n (one fewer than the input). The first observation has no preceding value, so it is[m
[32m+[m[32m   **omitted**; it is not filled with 0 or NaN.[m
[32m+[m[32m7. **Edge cases and limitations.** Constant values give zero returns. The pandas index is not[m
[32m+[m[32m   preserved. Cash flows (deposits or withdrawals) are not handled; the input must be a[m
[32m+[m[32m   self-financing value path. A total loss to exactly 0 cannot be represented and must be handled[m
[32m+[m[32m   by the caller or environment (e.g. by terminating the episode).[m
[32m+[m[32m8. **Tests.** Hand-calculated paths, including mixed positive and negative returns, integer input[m
[32m+[m[32m   and constant values; telescoping identity ∏(1 + r_t) = V_n / V_0; scale invariance; output[m
[32m+[m[32m   length, dtype and finiteness; rejection of zero, negative, NaN, inf, empty, single-value, 2-D and[m
[32m+[m[32m   non-numeric input.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 10.3 Annualised volatility: `annualized_volatility(returns, periods_per_year)`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Purpose.** Measures how much returns fluctuate: a basic measure of risk, comparable across[m
[32m+[m[32m   data frequencies once annualised.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Definition.** σ_ann = σ_period · √N, with σ_period = sqrt( Σ (r_t − r̄)² / (T − 1) ).[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Variables.** r_t are periodic returns, r̄ is their arithmetic mean, T is the number of[m
[32m+[m[32m   returns, and N = `periods_per_year`.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Assumptions and units.** Sample standard deviation (`ddof=1`), an unbiased variance estimator[m
[32m+[m[32m   for a sample. √N scaling assumes returns are independent and identically distributed;[m
[32m+[m[32m   autocorrelation (e.g. trending or mean-reverting returns) makes it inexact. Output is an annual[m
[32m+[m[32m   decimal (0.20 = 20 % per year).[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Example.** r = [0.01, −0.01, 0.02, 0.00]. The mean is 0.005; the squared deviations sum to[m
[32m+[m[32m   5 × 10⁻⁴; the sample variance is 5 × 10⁻⁴ / 3. With N = 252: σ_ann = √(5 × 10⁻⁴ / 3 × 252)[m
[32m+[m[32m   = √0.042 ≈ 0.2049.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. **Contract.** Input: at least 2 finite returns, each ≥ −1, and a positive finite N. Output: a[m
[32m+[m[32m   non-negative Python `float`. Returns exactly 0.0 when σ_period ≤ 1e-12.[m
[32m+[m[32m7. **Edge cases and limitations.** Constant returns give 0.0. One return is rejected because the[m
[32m+[m[32m   sample std needs at least 2. Returns below −1 are rejected as probable percentage-unit errors.[m
[32m+[m[32m   Choosing N is the caller's responsibility; the project-wide choice per frequency is open (D-023).[m
[32m+[m[32m8. **Tests.** Three hand-computed cases (N = 4, 12, 252); an explicit check that ddof = 1 differs[m
[32m+[m[32m   from ddof = 0; √N scaling (N × 4 doubles σ); constant returns give exactly 0; total-loss[m
[32m+[m[32m   return −1 is accepted; non-integer N; invalid N (0, negative, NaN, ±inf, bool, string, None,[m
[32m+[m[32m   list).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 10.4 Sharpe ratio: `sharpe_ratio(returns, periods_per_year, *, annual_risk_free_rate=None, periodic_risk_free_rate=None)`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Purpose.** Risk-adjusted performance: average return in excess of a risk-free rate, per unit of[m
[32m+[m[32m   volatility. One of the abstract's core metrics.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Definition.** S_ann = √N · mean(r_t − r_f,t) / std(r_t − r_f,t), with std computed using `ddof=1`.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Variables.** r_t are periodic returns, r_f,t is the **periodic** risk-free rate, and N =[m
[32m+[m[32m   `periods_per_year`.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Assumptions and units.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - The risk-free rate must match the return frequency. An annual rate R is converted[m
[32m+[m[32m     geometrically: r_f = (1 + R)^(1/N) − 1, so that compounding N periods gives back R exactly[m
[32m+[m[32m     (`annual_to_periodic_rate`). An annual rate is never subtracted directly from periodic returns.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Supply at most one of `annual_risk_free_rate` (a scalar) and `periodic_risk_free_rate` (a scalar[m
[32m+[m[32m     or one value per return). If neither is given, the rate is 0.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Arithmetic mean; √N annualisation assumes i.i.d. returns. The output is dimensionless.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Config `environment.risk_free_rate` is an annual decimal, so pass it as `annual_risk_free_rate`.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Example.** r = [0.02, 0.04, 0.00] with N = 12 and an annual rf of 1.01¹² − 1 ≈ 12.68 %, which[m
[32m+[m[32m   converts to exactly 0.01 per month. Excess returns are [0.01, 0.03, −0.01], with mean 0.01 and[m
[32m+[m[32m   sample std 0.02, giving a periodic Sharpe of 0.5. S_ann = 0.5 · √12 ≈ 1.732. Simple division[m
[32m+[m[32m   (12.68 % / 12) would instead give ≈ 1.634.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. **Contract.** Input: at least 2 valid returns and a positive finite N. Rates must be finite and[m
[32m+[m[32m   greater than −1, and a periodic array must have the same length as the returns. Output: a Python[m
[32m+[m[32m   `float`, which may be negative.[m
[32m+[m[32m7. **Edge cases and limitations.** If the std of excess returns is ≤ 1e-12, the ratio is undefined[m
[32m+[m[32m   and the function raises `UndefinedMetricError`. This also catches mathematically constant excess[m
[32m+[m[32m   returns that floating-point arithmetic turns into ~1e-18 noise. Supplying both rate forms is an[m
[32m+[m[32m   error. The Sharpe ratio penalises upside and downside volatility equally and ignores fat tails;[m
[32m+[m[32m   short samples give noisy estimates.[m
[32m+[m[32m8. **Tests.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Hand-computed values: √12 with no risk-free rate; −√12 for mirrored returns; √3 with an annual[m
[32m+[m[32m     rf (and a check that the simple-division answer is *not* returned); √3 with a scalar periodic[m
[32m+[m[32m     rf; exactly 4 with a time-varying rf.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Equivalence of the zero-rf forms.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - `UndefinedMetricError` for constant returns and for constant excess returns.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Rejection of: both rf forms; rf ≤ −1, NaN or ±inf; length mismatch; non-numeric rf; invalid N.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 10.5 Maximum drawdown: `max_drawdown(portfolio_values)` and `drawdown_series(portfolio_values)`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Purpose.** The worst loss from a previous high: what an investor who bought at the worst time[m
[32m+[m[32m   would have suffered. A core risk metric in the abstract.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Definition.** P_t = max_{s ≤ t} V_s, D_t = V_t / P_t − 1, MDD = min_t D_t.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Variables.** V_t is the portfolio value, P_t the running peak, and D_t the drawdown at t[m
[32m+[m[32m   (≤ 0).[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Assumptions and units.** The **first observation is the initial peak** (D_0 = 0). Any[m
[32m+[m[32m   decline that started before the series is invisible. Output is a non-positive decimal (−0.25 =[m
[32m+[m[32m   a 25 % decline).[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Example.** V = [100, 120, 90, 110, 130, 117] gives P = [100, 120, 120, 120, 130, 130] and[m
[32m+[m[32m   D = [0, 0, −0.25, −0.0833, 0, −0.10]. MDD = −0.25, with the peak at index 1 (120) and the trough[m
[32m+[m[32m   at index 2 (90). The path then recovers to a new high (130).[m
[32m+[m[32m6. **Contract.** Input: at least 2 finite, positive values. `drawdown_series` returns a float64[m
[32m+[m[32m   array of the same length. `max_drawdown` returns `MaxDrawdown(max_drawdown: float,[m
[32m+[m[32m   peak_index: int, trough_index: int)`. With no decline, the result is 0.0 and both indices are 0.[m
[32m+[m[32m   Ties: the **earliest** deepest point is the trough; the **latest** observation at the running[m
[32m+[m[32m   peak before the trough is the peak (where the decline began).[m
[32m+[m[32m7. **Edge cases and limitations.** Monotonically rising or constant paths give 0.0. The result[m
[32m+[m[32m   satisfies −1 < MDD ≤ 0. Drawdown duration and recovery time are not reported. Sampling frequency[m
[32m+[m[32m   matters: an intraday trough is invisible in daily data.[m
[32m+[m[32m8. **Tests.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - The hand-computed drawdown series for the recovery path above.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - MDD with recovery, a decline from the start, no decline, and constant values.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Tie-breaking: the latest peak among equal highs, and the earliest of equal troughs.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Scale invariance; bounds; output types; non-mutation of the input; shared invalid-input[m
[32m+[m[32m     rejection.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 10.6 Cumulative return: `cumulative_return(portfolio_values)`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Purpose.** The total gain or loss over the whole evaluation window, the most intuitive[m
[32m+[m[32m   performance number. It is named in the abstract.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Definition.** R_cum = V_T / V_0 − 1.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Variables.** V_0 is the first portfolio value, V_T is the last, and T is the number of[m
[32m+[m[32m   periods.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Assumptions and units.** The value path is self-financing (no deposits or withdrawals). The[m
[32m+[m[32m   result is a decimal (0.21 = +21 %), and is always > −1 for positive values.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Example.** V = [100, 110, 99, 121] gives 121/100 − 1 = **0.21**. Equivalently, the returns[m
[32m+[m[32m   [0.10, −0.10, 0.2222…] compound to 1.10 × 0.90 × 1.2222… = 1.21.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. **Contract.** Input: at least 2 finite, strictly positive values. Output: a Python `float`.[m
[32m+[m[32m7. **Edge cases and limitations.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - A path that ends where it started gives 0.0, however volatile it was in between.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Intermediate values do not affect the result, but are still validated (NaN or ≤ 0 anywhere[m
[32m+[m[32m     raises).[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Cumulative return ignores both the length of the window and the risk taken. Always report it[m
[32m+[m[32m     with T, volatility and drawdown.[m
[32m+[m[32m8. **Tests** (`tests/test_metrics.py`, section E):[m
[32m+[m[32m   - positive (+0.21), negative (−0.10) and zero results;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - equality with ∏(1 + r_t) − 1 computed from `portfolio_returns`;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - scale invariance, and a decimal (not percentage) result;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - rejection of corrupt intermediate values;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - shared invalid-input tests (types, empty, single value, NaN/inf, ≤ 0, 2-D).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 10.7 Annualised return (CAGR): `annualized_return(portfolio_values, periods_per_year)`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Purpose.** Puts windows of different lengths on a common per-year scale. It is the[m
[32m+[m[32m   compounded growth rate an investor actually experienced.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Definition.** R_ann = (V_T / V_0)^(N/T) − 1, computed as `expm1((N/T)·ln(V_T/V_0))`.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Variables.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - V_0, V_T: the first and last values.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - T: the number of observed return periods (number of values − 1).[m
[32m+[m[32m   - N: `periods_per_year`.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - T/N is the window length in years.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Assumptions and units.** The result is a decimal per year. N is explicit, with no daily[m
[32m+[m[32m   default (D-023). The method is geometric (D-029).[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Example.** 24 monthly periods (N = 12) from 100 to 121: (1.21)^(12/24) − 1 = 1.1 − 1 =[m
[32m+[m[32m   **0.10** per year, whatever the path in between.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **Geometric vs. arithmetic:** 100 → 150 → 75 with N = 1. The arithmetic mean return is[m
[32m+[m[32m     (0.5 − 0.5)/2 = 0, so mean × N = 0. CAGR is √0.75 − 1 ≈ **−0.134**. The portfolio really lost[m
[32m+[m[32m     25 % over two years; the arithmetic figure hides this loss. In general, CAGR ≈ arithmetic[m
[32m+[m[32m     mean − σ²/2 per period ("volatility drag").[m
[32m+[m[32m6. **Contract.** Input: at least 2 finite, strictly positive values (T ≥ 1) and a positive,[m
[32m+[m[32m   finite N. Output: a Python `float` > −1.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Extreme short-period losses may round to exactly −1.0.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - A result too large to represent (e.g. a 1e6-fold gain in one daily period) raises[m
[32m+[m[32m     `ValueError`.[m
[32m+[m[32m7. **Edge cases and limitations.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **Short windows are misleading.** Annualising extrapolates: one month of +5 % gives[m
[32m+[m[32m     1.05¹² − 1 ≈ **+79.6 %** per year. The formula does not correct this, and no minimum length is[m
[32m+[m[32m     enforced. The proposed rule (D-029) is to state T and the dates, and not to headline windows[m
[32m+[m[32m     shorter than one year.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Only V_0, V_T and T matter.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - When T = N (exactly one year), CAGR equals the cumulative return.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - CAGR is not the same quantity as the arithmetic mean in the Sharpe numerator. Do not mix them.[m
[32m+[m[32m8. **Tests** (`tests/test_metrics.py`, section F):[m
[32m+[m[32m   - hand-computed 0.10 for yearly (T = 2), single-period and 24-month paths (smooth and zigzag,[m
[32m+[m[32m     which confirms path independence);[m
[32m+[m[32m   - −0.10 for a declining path;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - fractional N (2.5);[m
[32m+[m[32m   - equality with cumulative return when T = N;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - the geometric-vs-arithmetic case;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - the short-window extrapolation (documented, not fixed);[m
[32m+[m[32m   - constant values give 0;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - overflow raises; underflow gives −1.0;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - invalid N (values and types).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 10.8 Portfolio turnover: `portfolio_turnover(pre_trade_weights, post_trade_weights, *, cash_column=None)`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Purpose.** Measures how much a strategy trades, which drives transaction costs. It is a core[m
[32m+[m[32m   metric in the abstract.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Definition** (two-way, D-011, D-030). Two measures, selected explicitly:[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **Default, `cash_column=None`:** τ_k = Σ_{i=1..A} |w_post[k, i] − w_pre[k, i]|, summed over[m
[32m+[m[32m     **every** column. This is unchanged from the original API.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **Traded notional, `cash_column=j`:** n_k = Σ_{i≠j} |w_post[k, i] − w_pre[k, i]|, summed over[m
[32m+[m[32m     **non-cash** columns only. Cash is the settlement account, not a traded security.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **Relationship:** let B and S be the total non-cash weight bought and sold, with a cash column[m
[32m+[m[32m     and rows summing to 1. The weight changes sum to 0, so |Δw_cash| = |B − S|. Therefore:[m
[32m+[m[32m     - default τ = B + S + |B − S| = **2·max(B, S)**;[m
[32m+[m[32m     - traded notional n = **B + S** = τ − |Δw_cash|;[m
[32m+[m[32m     - one-way turnover = τ / 2 = **max(B, S)**;[m
[32m+[m[32m     - so **one-way ≤ traded notional ≤ default two-way**.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **Without a cash column** (fully invested portfolio), B = S, so the default already equals[m
[32m+[m[32m     traded notional and `cash_column` is unnecessary.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Always state which measure a reported number uses.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Variables.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - k: a rebalance event (one row); A: the number of columns, including cash if it is a column.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - j: the 0-based index of the cash column.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - w_pre[k, i]: the **actual** weight of asset i immediately before trading, after market drift.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - w_post[k, i]: the target weight immediately after trading.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Assumptions and units.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Weights are fractions of portfolio value.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Long-only: each weight is ≥ 0 and each row sums to 1 within `WEIGHT_SUM_TOLERANCE` (1e-6).[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Both matrices use the same asset order, and both include (or both exclude) a cash column.[m
[32m+[m[32m     With `allow_cash: true`, cash must be an explicit column.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - τ, n ∈ [0, 2]: 0 means no trade; 2 means the whole portfolio was replaced.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - The function is timing-agnostic. The caller measures w_pre at the execution time set by D-013.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - It computes no transaction costs. Which measure costs are charged on is open (D-031), to be[m
[32m+[m[32m     implemented and validated with the environment.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Examples.** Columns are [A, B, CASH] and pre-trade weights are [0.5, 0.3, 0.2], unless stated[m
[32m+[m[32m   otherwise.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   | Trade | Default (all columns) | `cash_column=2` (traded notional) |[m
[32m+[m[32m   | --- | --- | --- |[m
[32m+[m[32m   | Buy 0.10 of A with cash → [0.6, 0.3, 0.1] | 0.1 + 0 + 0.1 = **0.20** | 0.1 + 0 = **0.10** |[m
[32m+[m[32m   | Switch 0.10 from A to B → [0.4, 0.4, 0.2] | **0.20** | **0.20** |[m
[32m+[m[32m   | Sell 0.1 of A, buy 0.2 of B → [0.4, 0.5, 0.1] | **0.40** (= 2·max(0.2, 0.1)) | **0.30** (= 0.2 + 0.1) |[m
[32m+[m[32m   | Initial funding [0, 0, 1] → [0.5, 0.5, 0] | **2.0** | **1.0** |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   - 60/40 → 50/50 with no cash column gives |−0.1| + |0.1| = **0.20** under both measures.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Asset A → asset B entirely gives **2.0**.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **Why drift matters:** the target is 50/50 at both rebalances. Asset A gains 10 % and B is[m
[32m+[m[32m     flat, so the weights drift to 11/21 and 10/21. Returning to 50/50 needs τ = 1/21 ≈ **0.048**.[m
[32m+[m[32m     Comparing consecutive targets (50/50 vs. 50/50) would wrongly report **0**, and therefore no[m
[32m+[m[32m     cost.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. **Contract.** Two matrices of shape (events, assets); a single event has shape (1, assets).[m
[32m+[m[32m   Output: a float64 array of length `events`.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - `cash_column` is keyword-only: `None` (default), or a non-negative integer index (Python or[m
[32m+[m[32m     NumPy integer).[m
[32m+[m[32m   - With `cash_column`, the **complete** rows, cash included, are still validated: finite,[m
[32m+[m[32m     non-negative, summing to 1. The cash column is excluded from the sum, not from validation.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - The function does **not** infer drift, dates or asset returns.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Initial funding from cash counts only if the caller supplies it as a row.[m
[32m+[m[32m7. **Edge cases and limitations.** Errors are raised for:[m
[32m+[m[32m   - empty matrices; 1-D, 3-D or scalar input; shape mismatch;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - NaN/inf; negative weights ("only long-only weights are supported");[m
[32m+[m[32m   - rows not summing to 1 (the message suggests adding a cash column); non-numeric input;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - `cash_column` that is not an integer (`TypeError`, booleans included), or outside[m
[32m+[m[32m     [0, assets − 1] (`ValueError`, negative indices included).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   Zero-trade events give exactly 0. A portfolio with only a cash column gives 0 with[m
[32m+[m[32m   `cash_column=0`. Not supported: shorting or leverage, and external cash flows. The function[m
[32m+[m[32m   cannot verify that column j really is cash; that is the caller's responsibility.[m
[32m+[m[32m   **Open (D-031):** how transaction costs use these measures. The proposed direction is to charge[m
[32m+[m[32m   on traded notional (`cash_column` set); not implemented in this milestone.[m
[32m+[m[32m8. **Tests** (`tests/test_turnover.py`):[m
[32m+[m[32m   - hand-computed partial (0.2), full (2.0) and zero-trade events; row order;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - two drift demonstrations: drift *adds* trading (1/21 vs. a naive 0), and drift can *reduce*[m
[32m+[m[32m     it (2 × 0.05/0.98 ≈ 0.102 vs. a naive 0.2);[m
[32m+[m[32m   - the cash leg counts in the default; an omitted cash column is detected; initial funding only[m
[32m+[m[32m     when supplied;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - bounds and symmetry on 200 random Dirichlet weight rows (seeded);[m
[32m+[m[32m   - a single-asset portfolio never trades;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - consistency with the config cap (the maximum turnover of 2.0 is a valid `max_turnover`);[m
[32m+[m[32m   - the weight-sum tolerance (accepted within, float32 accepted, rejected beyond);[m
[32m+[m[32m   - all invalid inputs; tuple and pandas DataFrame input; no mutation of the inputs;[m
[32m+[m[32m   - **`cash_column`:**[m
[32m+[m[32m     - the four examples in the table above, plus multi-event rows;[m
[32m+[m[32m     - cash as the first column; a NumPy integer index; a cash-only portfolio;[m
[32m+[m[32m     - the identities n = B + S, τ = 2·max(B, S) and n = τ − |Δw_cash|, with[m
[32m+[m[32m       one-way ≤ n ≤ τ, on 300 seeded random rows;[m
[32m+[m[32m     - legacy default preserved (omitted = `None` = the all-column sum);[m
[32m+[m[32m     - invalid indices (−1, −3, 3, 10; 2.0, "2", `True`, `np.bool_`, `[2]`);[m
[32m+[m[32m     - full-row validation still applied (row sum, negative cash, omitted cash column).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 10.9 Annualised turnover: `annualized_turnover(event_turnover, observation_periods, periods_per_year)`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Purpose.** A single comparable figure ("the strategy trades 150 % of its value per year"),[m
[32m+[m[32m   independent of how often it rebalances.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Definition.** Annual turnover = Σ_k τ_k · N / T_obs.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Variables.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - τ_k: per-event turnover from §10.8.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - T_obs: the number of return periods in the evaluation window (not the number of events).[m
[32m+[m[32m   - N: `periods_per_year`.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Assumptions and units.** Per year, as a decimal. Events must all fall within the window. The[m
[32m+[m[32m   result uses the same measure as its input (default two-way, or traded notional if the events[m
[32m+[m[32m   came from `portfolio_turnover(..., cash_column=j)`), so report which one was used.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Example.** 12 monthly rebalances of 0.10 within 252 daily periods (N = 252): 1.2 × 252/252 =[m
[32m+[m[32m   **1.2** per year. 6 events of 0.2 over 24 months (N = 12): 1.2 × 12/24 = **0.6** per year.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. **Contract.**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - `event_turnover` is 1-D, with values in [0, 2]. An empty list gives **0.0**, because no[m
[32m+[m[32m     rebalancing means no trading (a deliberate, documented exception to "empty raises").[m
[32m+[m[32m   - `observation_periods` is a positive integer (Python or NumPy): `TypeError` for non-integers[m
[32m+[m[32m     or booleans, `ValueError` for ≤ 0.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - N is validated as elsewhere.[m
[32m+[m[32m   - The return value is always a Python `float`, including for NumPy integer[m
[32m+[m[32m     `observation_periods` (regression-tested).[m
[32m+[m[32m7. **Limitations.** It cannot check that the events really lie inside the window; the caller[m
[32m+[m[32m   supplies consistent inputs. Annualising a short window has the same extrapolation problem as[m
[32m+[m[32m   §10.7.[m
[32m+[m[32m8. **Tests:** the two examples above; agreement with `portfolio_turnover` output; empty input[m
[32m+[m[32m   gives 0; out-of-range or non-finite event values; 2-D input; invalid `observation_periods`[m
[32m+[m[32m   (values and types); invalid N; the return type is `float` for `int`, `np.int64`, `np.int32` and[m
[32m+[m[32m   `np.uint16` periods.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 10.10 Consistency across all metrics[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Property | How it holds |[m
[32m+[m[32m| --- | --- |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Decimal units | Every return, rate, volatility, drawdown and turnover is a decimal. Returns < −1 are rejected as probable percentages. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Explicit annualisation | `periods_per_year` is a required argument of every annualised metric; there are no defaults. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Risk-free handling | Only the Sharpe ratio uses a risk-free rate. An annual rate is converted geometrically (D-024). |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Drawdown sign | `max_drawdown` ≤ 0 and > −1 (tested). |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Turnover | Two-way, with values in [0, 2] for both measures, matching the config's `max_turnover ∈ (0, 2]` (tested for the default measure). The default sums all columns; `cash_column` gives traded notional. **Which measure the config cap constrains is not yet decided** (it stays with D-031); the config comment describes the default. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Invalid input | Errors are raised; nothing is cleaned silently. The one documented exception is that empty turnover events give 0. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Public API | All existing signatures and defaults are unchanged. `cash_column` is a new keyword-only argument whose default reproduces the earlier behaviour; the full pre-existing suite still passes. |[m
